{"id":"6364723ca702a8e6","group":"58","path":"58/batch19/58-thm-taniyama-shimura.md","title":"Taniyama–Shimura Conjecture","display":"thm-taniyama-shimura — Taniyama–Shimura Conjecture","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-taniyama-shimura","aliases":["58-thm-taniyama-shimura"],"display":"thm-taniyama-shimura — Taniyama–Shimura Conjecture","depends_on":["[[58-df-modular-form]]","[[58-df-elliptic-curve]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-taniyama-shimura"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-taniyama-shimura</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-taniyama-shimura — Taniyama–Shimura Conjecture"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"a891b0f45131631a\" href=\"?note=a891b0f45131631a\" title=\"58-df-modular-form\">58-df-modular-form</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"74f4744df7db749f\" href=\"?note=74f4744df7db749f\" title=\"58-df-elliptic-curve\">58-df-elliptic-curve</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Explicit relation signatures used below: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{EllipticCurve}_S\\subseteq V^{4}\">\\(\\mathrm{EllipticCurve}_S\\subseteq V^{4}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CuspForm}_S\\subseteq V^{3}\">\\(\\mathrm{CuspForm}_S\\subseteq V^{3}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CuspExpansion}_S\\subseteq V^{6}\">\\(\\mathrm{CuspExpansion}_S\\subseteq V^{6}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ModularEllipticCurve}_S\\subseteq V^{3}\">\\(\\mathrm{ModularEllipticCurve}_S\\subseteq V^{3}\\)</span>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"E,O,K_E\\in V\">\\(E,O,K_E\\in V\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{EllipticCurve}_S(E,\\mathbb Q,O,K_E)\">\\(\\mathrm{EllipticCurve}_S(E,\\mathbb Q,O,K_E)\\)</span> is the elliptic-curve predicate from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"74f4744df7db749f\" href=\"?note=74f4744df7db749f\" title=\"58-df-elliptic-curve\">58-df-elliptic-curve</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S_2(\\Gamma_0(N))\">\\(S_2(\\Gamma_0(N))\\)</span> is the set of weight-<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"2\">\\(2\\)</span> cusp forms on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Gamma_0(N)\">\\(\\Gamma_0(N)\\)</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L(E,s)\">\\(L(E,s)\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L(f,s)\">\\(L(f,s)\\)</span> are the Hasse--Weil and cusp-form <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\">\\(L\\)</span>-series, respectively</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}modular\\text{-}elliptic\\text{-}curve}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{ModularEllipticCurve}_S(E,O,K_E)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{EllipticCurve}_S(E,\\mathbb Q,O,K_E)\n\\land\\exists N\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\exists f\\in S_2(\\Gamma_0(N))\\;\\exists a\\in\\mathbb C^\\omega\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{CuspForm}_S(f,2,\\Gamma_0(N))\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{45pt}\\land\\mathrm{CuspExpansion}_S(a,f,2,\\infty,I_2,1)\n\\land a(1)=1\n\\land\\forall s\\in\\mathbb C\\;\\bigl(\\operatorname{Re}(s)&gt;\\tfrac32\\to L(E,s)=L(f,s)\\bigr)\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}modular\\text{-}elliptic\\text{-}curve}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{ModularEllipticCurve}_S(E,O,K_E)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{EllipticCurve}_S(E,\\mathbb Q,O,K_E)\n\\land\\exists N\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\exists f\\in S_2(\\Gamma_0(N))\\;\\exists a\\in\\mathbb C^\\omega\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{CuspForm}_S(f,2,\\Gamma_0(N))\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{45pt}\\land\\mathrm{CuspExpansion}_S(a,f,2,\\infty,I_2,1)\n\\land a(1)=1\n\\land\\forall s\\in\\mathbb C\\;\\bigl(\\operatorname{Re}(s)&gt;\\tfrac32\\to L(E,s)=L(f,s)\\bigr)\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}taniyama\\text{-}shimura} \\vdash \\forall E,O,K_E\\in V\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{EllipticCurve}_S(E,\\mathbb Q,O,K_E)\\to\\mathrm{ModularEllipticCurve}_S(E,O,K_E)\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}taniyama\\text{-}shimura} \\vdash \\forall E,O,K_E\\in V\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{EllipticCurve}_S(E,\\mathbb Q,O,K_E)\\to\\mathrm{ModularEllipticCurve}_S(E,O,K_E)\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The theorem quantifies only over actual elliptic curves over <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb Q\">\\(\\mathbb Q\\)</span> and expands modularity into a normalized cusp-form witness with matching <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\">\\(L\\)</span>-series; no undefined <code>Modular</code> or <code>NormalizedNewform</code> predicate remains.</li>\n<li>Proven by Wiles (1994) for semistable curves, completed by Breuil–Conrad–Diamond–Taylor.</li>\n<li>Implies Fermat's Last Theorem: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"a^n + b^n = c^n\">\\(a^n + b^n = c^n\\)</span> has no nontrivial integer solutions for <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n &gt; 2\">\\(n &gt; 2\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Modularity implies analytic continuation and the expected functional equation for <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L(E,s)\">\\(L(E,s)\\)</span>; analytic continuation alone is not an equivalent definition of modularity.</li>\n<li>The conjecture generalizes to abelian varieties via modular forms.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-modular-form","status":"resolved","id":"a891b0f45131631a","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-modular-form]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-elliptic-curve","status":"resolved","id":"74f4744df7db749f","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-elliptic-curve]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-elliptic-curve","status":"resolved","id":"74f4744df7db749f","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$E,O,K_E\\in V$ and $\\mathrm{EllipticCurve}_S(E,\\mathbb Q,O,K_E)$ is the elliptic-curve predicate from [[58-df-elliptic-curve]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathrm{EllipticCurve}_S\\subseteq V^{4}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{CuspForm}_S\\subseteq V^{3}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{CuspExpansion}_S\\subseteq V^{6}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ModularEllipticCurve}_S\\subseteq V^{3}","display":false},{"tex":"E,O,K_E\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{EllipticCurve}_S(E,\\mathbb Q,O,K_E)","display":false},{"tex":"S_2(\\Gamma_0(N))","display":false},{"tex":"2","display":false},{"tex":"\\Gamma_0(N)","display":false},{"tex":"L(E,s)","display":false},{"tex":"L(f,s)","display":false},{"tex":"L","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}modular\\text{-}elliptic\\text{-}curve}\\vdash{}&\n\\mathrm{ModularEllipticCurve}_S(E,O,K_E)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&\n\\mathrm{EllipticCurve}_S(E,\\mathbb Q,O,K_E)\n\\land\\exists N\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\exists f\\in S_2(\\Gamma_0(N))\\;\\exists a\\in\\mathbb C^\\omega\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{CuspForm}_S(f,2,\\Gamma_0(N))\\\\\n&\\hspace{45pt}\\land\\mathrm{CuspExpansion}_S(a,f,2,\\infty,I_2,1)\n\\land a(1)=1\n\\land\\forall s\\in\\mathbb C\\;\\bigl(\\operatorname{Re}(s)>\\tfrac32\\to L(E,s)=L(f,s)\\bigr)\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}taniyama\\text{-}shimura} \\vdash \\forall E,O,K_E\\in V\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{EllipticCurve}_S(E,\\mathbb Q,O,K_E)\\to\\mathrm{ModularEllipticCurve}_S(E,O,K_E)\\bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathbb Q","display":false},{"tex":"L","display":false},{"tex":"a^n + b^n = c^n","display":false},{"tex":"n > 2","display":false},{"tex":"L(E,s)","display":false}],"bytes":2259,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4457","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch19/58-thm-taniyama-shimura.md|58-thm-taniyama-shimura]]（batch19）"}],"outgoing":["a891b0f45131631a","74f4744df7db749f"]}